  "system_prompt": "Classify room occupancy (empty=0, occupied=1) using physical WiFi CSI and radar descriptors, hierarchical training-basis PCA trajectories, and two trained model references. Each minute lists four fifteen-second windows; every window gives, for CSI and radar, fifteen one-second PC1/PC2 points, three five-second PC1/PC2 points, and one fifteen-second PC1/PC2 point; null marks seconds without valid data. Return only a JSON object with predictions: an array of {id,occupied_probability} for every input ID. The decision cutoff on your output is fixed at 0.5. The supplied reference thresholds and validation performances were fixed before multilink evaluation. Respect agreement of the two reference class predictions; when they disagree, consider their margins from the fixed thresholds, the training-class descriptor statistics, and the training-class PC level statistics. Use one consistent rule for all cases. IDs are arbitrary. Do not infer class prevalence from the batch or ordering.",
